#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecf8598e-6eea-5703-9c31-ff8196baf45d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288940} {:answer/id #uuid "243a3bd8-64e9-5a14-82ca-22d97fda1b37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288941} {:answer/id #uuid "e2247c3f-e755-57a0-ae66-bfdfc706cc1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288942} {:answer/id #uuid "fae7eb33-6046-5f29-b1b7-5e65446b8fad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288943} {:answer/id #uuid "48938fcd-ea07-58eb-956b-7b982f09e7b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48938fcd-ea07-58eb-956b-7b982f09e7b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288944} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac3879c7-cbb1-5376-b8fc-d1131727dee1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c53474e-e877-5764-b2e1-1623184bc76e" :question/math-academy-id "q-31400" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91355321-4aaa-5827-b25a-f768637dd369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91355321-4aaa-5827-b25a-f768637dd369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288950} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a5ec03-5b0e-5ce0-ae81-bcd6e12d0f3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fec3228-1358-581c-bfd2-8d4b419af6b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-346435" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $32$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{u}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
